Graph `app` examples for a page anchor, an incoming edge, an action on that page, and a task
that runs the action. The graph also needs a page anchor `app.entry` for the desktop.
Save each template in the bundle that uses it and set wait times from the observed frames.
For each input, identify the expected screen evidence. Keep the failing statement's error
when it already identifies the problem. When handling a failed check in a branch, log the
expected template and the step that reached it before returning false.

### Anchor `app.feed`

`golden.md` -- what the screen is, fixed parts and changing parts:

```text
---
kind: page
---
Home feed: the tab bar along the bottom (feed, search, inbox, profile) with the feed tab
lit, the app's logo top left. The posts, their pictures and the unread counts change.
```

`main.ccat` -- only judges whether that screen is showing:

```ccat
// The logo is a fixed control unique to the feed.
if (has("feed_logo.png")) { return true }
return false
```

### Edge `app.entry-feed`

`main.ccat` -- only the move. The engine checks it starts on `entry` and gives `feed`
20 s to show up afterwards, so it never checks its own ends and never calls `goto`:

```ccat
// From the desktop into the app. A cold start shows an inline sign-in step
// first; a warm start lands on the feed directly. Either way ends on the feed.
tap("app_icon.png")
log("app icon tapped; waiting for the startup screen")
wait(3000)                           // about twice the observed 1.5 s start-up time
if (has("sign_in.png")) {
  tap("sign_in.png")
  log("sign-in button tapped; waiting for the feed")
} else {
  log("no sign-in button matched after startup; waiting for the feed")
}
```

### Action `app.feed.claim`

`main.ccat` performs the daily claim and closes its single receipt. The graph engine checks
that the action starts and ends on `feed` and runs its body once. Keep the templates in
this action bundle.

```ccat
// Collects the daily reward, and says what it found.
defs {
  feed    = "feed.png"               // feed marker hidden by the receipt
  claim   = "claim.png"              // the enabled claim button
  taken   = "claimed.png"            // the same button, greyed out once it is collected
  popup   = "reward_popup.png"       // the receipt sheet that shows only after a claim lands
  close_x = "popup_close.png"        // its top-right X
}

// The button's text can match both templates. Give the completed state priority.
if (has(taken)) {
  log("already claimed today")
  return true
}
if (has(claim)) {
  tap(claim)
  log("claim button tapped; waiting for the reward receipt")
  if (wait_until(popup, 8000)) {
    log("reward receipt matched; closing it with popup_close.png")
  } else {
    log("reward_popup.png was not confirmed after tapping claim.png")
    return false
  }
  tap(close_x)
  log("receipt close button tapped; waiting for the feed marker")
  if (wait_until(feed, 4000)) {
    log("feed marker matched after closing the receipt; checking the claimed state")
  } else {
    log("feed.png was not confirmed after tapping popup_close.png")
    return false
  }
  if (wait_until(taken, 4000)) {
    log("daily claim done")
    return true
  } else {
    log("claimed.png was not confirmed after returning to the feed")
    return false
  }
}

log("neither claimed.png nor claim.png matched on the feed")
return false
```

### Task `app.daily_claim`

`main.ccat` -- `goto` the page and `run` the graph action. The action logs its progress and
the engine checks its result. On failure, use the returned error and the last script log
to find the failing step.

```ccat
// A task walks to the screen first. The graph checks both ends of every hop,
// so arriving is already confirmed; a screen it cannot reach is an error that
// names the hops, and the action does not run against the wrong screen.
goto("app:feed")
log("feed confirmed; running app.feed.claim")

// A standalone run preserves uncaught errors. Action logs identify handled failures.
run("app.feed.claim/main.ccat")
log("app.feed.claim succeeded; return to the feed confirmed")
return true
```
